A||||9||spike||My car just died, Please help||||9||
Z||000000||spike||08-11-2000||09:57 PM||||Well here's what happened. I was driving along with the headlights, radio and the heater (cold air) on. I just made it across the bridge and WHAM the car just died. It costed to a stop and nothing electric would work except for the headlights. I am sure I heard a pop but then again I'm not 100% sure. I checked all the fuses and the battery conection and all seemed fine. I had to have it towed to the nearest garage. I am not really all that happy where it is, but I had no choice. Does anyone have any ideas what the problem may be.<P>Thanks for your help, Mike. ||||reg||9
Z||000001||My7Fieros||08-11-2000||10:24 PM||||Depends....did your car start right back up? If the answer is no, then its your distributor pick up coil and/or ignition control module.<BR>The exact same thing happend to me. People here on the forum told me a few things, mostly the above mentioned. Sure enough, that was it.<BR>What happends is it gets icky and corroded..when it gets hot...whammo, it shuts down,therefore not producing a spark, not to restart for a couple of hours (until it cools). Its an easy fix, and cheap to.<BR>Judging by the limited info you gave, that would be my guess.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by My7Fieros (edited 08-11-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||WisconsinGT||08-11-2000||10:45 PM||||Mike, My7 is right on the money. I had the exact same problem. Change the ignition control module inside your distributor. See if that cures your ills. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Taijiguy||08-11-2000||10:50 PM||||The only problem with the ignition control module diagnoses, is that if it fails, it doesn't take out everything else electrical with it. He stated in his post the only thing electrical that work was the headlights. SOunds like something more basically electrtical than the ignition control module, like a fusible link, or even a ground wire. <P>-Taiji||||reg||1
Z||000004||DaRkLoRD||08-11-2000||10:50 PM||||Since he had to get it towed to a garage.. I'm assuming it didn't start right up again.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>but I could be wrong.. after all, if my car died like that.. I'd probably get it towed as well, so I wouldn't risk driving it just in case there was a serious problem!<P>------------------<BR> <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A> <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||1
Z||000005||spike||08-11-2000||10:57 PM||||Thank you for the quick response. The car will not start at all. It does nothing, but on the good side the headlights work. Well I hope that it is as simple as that. The bill won't be too high or at least it better not be! I have not found a trust worthy garage yet. I will just have to wait and see what they say the problem is.<P>Thanks, Mike.<BR>85 Fiero SE Duke (Converted to FB)<BR>Presently ill.<BR>||||reg||7
Z||000006||Oreif||08-12-2000||12:58 AM||||By "won't start but headlights  work" Do you mean the engine won't even turn over? If that is the case It might be a fuse link went bad. If the engine turns over but doesn't run then look at the above mentioned ignition items. If you have no power to the engine it's most likely a bad fuse link.||||reg||1
Z||000007||fierospeeder||08-12-2000||05:28 AM||||i had this happen to my tbird, but my battery died out, it was during a snow storm.  <P>I was lucky there was a car store near by, and i had my tools.<BR>Try jumping it and see if she runs, and also if your alternators putting out 14 volts.||||reg||1
Z||000008||spike||08-12-2000||06:51 AM||||The car won't turn over. It seems to have no power. When key is turned it does nothing at all. I am wondering if I should call them and tell them to check the ignition and pick-up coil. I have always found that garages don't like to be told what the problem is.<P>Thanks, Mike.||||reg||1
Z||000009||88formula||08-13-2000||08:43 PM||||If you have no power to things like the radio and interior accessories but the headlights work than I tend to agree with Taijiguy. You probably have a broken or corroded fusible link or ground strap.||||reg||1
